{"step_index":609,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-05T00:18:33Z","content":"To get this working on another PC, everything is already backed up to **OneDrive** and **GitHub** with a **1-click restore file**. \n\nHere is how you do it:\n\n---\n\n### Method 1: Using OneDrive (Fastest)\n\nIf your new PC is signed into your Microsoft / OneDrive account:\n\n1. Open your File Explorer and go to:\n   ```text\n   OneDrive > RLCF-Video-Automation-Backup\n   ```\n2. Double-click **`Install_On_New_PC.bat`**.\n3. **Done!** Open DaVinci Resolve, and all your scripts will immediately appear under:\n   > **Workspace** $\\rightarrow$ **Scripts** $\\rightarrow$ **Edit**\n\n---\n\n### Method 2: Using GitHub (Any PC)\n\nIf the PC does not have your OneDrive connected:\n\n1. On the new PC, go to your GitHub repository:\n   👉 **[https://github.com/davelane26/rlcf-video-automation](https://github.com/davelane26/rlcf-video-automation)**\n2. Click the green **Code** button $\\rightarrow$ **Download ZIP**.\n3. Extract/Unzip the folder.\n4. Double-click **`Install_On_New_PC.bat`**.\n5. **Done!**\n\n---\n\n### What `Install_On_New_PC.bat` Does Automatically:\n- Copies all timeline scripts into DaVinci Resolve's system directory:\n  `%APPDATA%\\Blackmagic Design\\DaVinci Resolve\\Support\\Fusion\\Scripts\\Edit\\`\n- Installs the **Antigravity Custom Skill** (`rlcf-video-editing`) into:\n  `%USERPROFILE%\\.gemini\\config\\skills\\rlcf-video-editing\\`\n\n---\n\n### 💡 If You Want Antigravity to Process *New* Sunday Meetings on the Other PC:\nIf you want to use Antigravity on that second computer to analyze future livestreams, ensure the new PC has:\n1. **DaVinci Resolve** installed.\n2. **Python** installed with the audio tools:\n   ```powershell\n   pip install faster-whisper scipy numpy\n   ```\n3. **FFmpeg** installed (or present in `Presenter` or added to your system PATH).\n\nOnce `Install_On_New_PC.bat` has been run, Antigravity on the new PC will automatically know the exact RLCF service format, song structures, and DaVinci Resolve scripting workflow.","thinking":"To run existing scripts on a new PC, there are two primary methods to consider. One uses a pre-existing OneDrive folder if available, allowing a simple batch file execution. The other option involves obtaining the scripts from a repository.\n\n\n"}
